 "budget": {
  "doc": "Tracing cost grows with the number of layers and with the size and boundary of each: a video crop of line art or paper grain gives hundreds of layers and one free path of 25000 px costs more than ten CPU minutes. The layers are ranked by area; only the largest maxRefined that stay under maxBoundaryPx of boundary and maxAreaPx of area are fitted with primitives and least squares, the others get the unrefined Bezier contour (cheap), and a layer under specklePx is never traced and is reported as a residual speck, never as a vector. A layer that spends layerCpuS seconds of CPU time (not wall time: a loaded machine does not change the result) keeps its unrefined contour and says so. The whole scene has an allowance of sceneCpuS CPU seconds shared by the pool, biggest layers first: once it is spent the layers not yet started keep the unrefined contour and say so (fit.budget scene-cpu). 14 October 2026: one hand-drawn line-art frame spent 2600 CPU seconds in the layers alone. FR : plafond de cout du trace, par couche et par scene. 14 October 2026: the layers whose boundary is at most rankFreeBoundaryPx (glyphs, icons: seconds each, tenths of IoU) are exempt from the maxRefined rank cap, run FIRST, cheapest first, and may spend at most shortShare of sceneCpuS so the big layers behind them are not starved (x-anabology S44: short layers alone took the whole allowance, 112 layers flagged scene-cpu and the cards at IoU 0.65). FR : contours courts d'abord, avec une part de l'enveloppe.",
